  <constraints>
    <constraint type="safety">Pruning ONLY happens after deployment — never during active development (AC #8). Auto-prune must validate it is called from deployment pipeline context.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency-check">A superseded node is NOT pruned if any active node depends on it. The Cypher query must check for incoming DEPENDS_ON edges from active nodes.</constraint>
    <constraint type="reversibility">Archived articles retain full content — pruning is reversible. Articles are moved, not deleted. The S3 backup includes the archive/ directory.</constraint>
    <constraint type="naming">Archived files use flat naming convention: {phase}--{slug}.md to avoid recreating phase subdirectories inside archive/.</constraint>
    <constraint type="ordering">Pruning runs AFTER deploy-nodes agent step (which marks code as deployed) and BEFORE final graph-sync (so the sync reflects the pruned state).</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">This story depends on Epic 2 (story compilation) and Story 3.3 (deployment compilation pipeline provides the trigger for pruning).</constraint>
    <constraint type="memgraph">DETACH DELETE removes the node AND all its edges. This is irreversible in Memgraph — the graph-sync can rebuild from wiki files if needed, but pruned articles are in archive/ and won't be synced.</constraint>
  </constraints>

